  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mapping of water catchment in Grootvlei area study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the development of an integral transition plan in Grootvlei and the greater Dipaleseng Local Municipality. This entails, amongst others, a clear understanding of the ecological and spatial situation to determine the basis for realistic, sustainable socio-economic pathways for the area. This will provide the basis of realistic sustainable pathways for the area.South Africa is a water scarce country, it receives on average half of the global average rainfall. Water in the South African context is, therefore, the enabling factor for socio-economic development, the welfare of rural and urban communities as well as the natural environment. A just transition pathway and integrated approach needs to take into account the possibilities and limitations of the available surface and ground water in the catchments relevant to Dipaleseng-Grootvlei.</narrative>
  </description>
